# Append this to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile. Do not replace the file: the push
# server's blocks are already in there, and losing them takes the iOS doorbell
# with them.
#
# A relay is a WebSocket and Caddy's reverse_proxy upgrades one without being
# told to, so there is nothing here about Connection or Upgrade headers.
#
# **keepalive off, and that is not a preference.** strfry's HTTP side is the
# small server built into uWebSockets, and it does not hold a connection the
# way Caddy's pool expects. With keep-alive on, every plain HTTP request came
# back to Caddy as an "Unsolicited response received on idle HTTP channel" and
# was thrown away — so `curl https://relay.cubechat.tech` returned nothing at
# all while the relay behind it was answering perfectly. The WebSocket upgrade
# is a fresh connection either way, so nothing about the actual traffic pays
# for this.
#
# X-Forwarded-For is not set here either: Caddy passes it by default and says
# so out loud when told to do it twice.

relay.cubechat.tech {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8081 {
		transport http {
			versions 1.1
			keepalive off
		}
	}
}
